    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following. $\\dfrac2x+\\dfrac3{x-1}$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{5x-2}{x(x-1)}$, $x\\ne0,1$.",
      "worked": "The original denominators require $x\\ne0,1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac2x+\\frac3{x-1}&=\\frac{2(x-1)+3x}{x(x-1)}\\\\\\frac2x+\\frac3{x-1}&=\\frac{5x-2}{x(x-1)}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
